# Template only. Copy to .env and fill in values locally.
# .env is gitignored and must never be committed. Values are never printed,
# logged, or pasted into source — not even sandbox ones.
#
# Two Windows footguns, both of which fail SILENTLY:
#
# 1. UTF-8 BOM voids the first variable.
#    If .env is saved as "UTF-8 with BOM", the three BOM bytes are prepended
#    to the first key name. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY below is then parsed as
#    "<BOM>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY" and reads back undefined, while every later
#    variable loads fine — so it looks like one key is bad rather than one
#    encoding is wrong. Save as plain "UTF-8" (no BOM).
#    Check the first three bytes in PowerShell:
#      Format-Hex .env -Count 3
#    EF BB BF means a BOM is present. Re-save without it.
#
# 2. Notepad silently appends .txt.
#    Saving this as ".env" in Notepad produces ".env.txt", which dotenv does
#    not load and .gitignore does still ignore — so nothing looks broken and
#    nothing works. In the Save dialog set "Save as type" to "All Files", or
#    create the file from the shell instead.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
PRAVA_SK=
